        "PMC11203300::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11413244::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing the electronegativity difference will decrease local lattice distortions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing the electronegativity difference will decrease localized bonding inhomogeneities.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced lattice distortion and bonding inhomogeneity will enhance dislocation mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced dislocation mobility will improve room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solid-solution strengthening will allow the modified alloy to retain high strength.",
